<title>AUSTRALIA: Adel Brighton settles Hawaiian Cement sale.</title>
<headline>Adel Brighton settles Hawaiian Cement sale.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian cement manufacturer Adelaide Brighton Ltd said it had settled the sale of its general partnership interest in Hawaiian Cement, announced in late May.</p>
<p>The proceeds of US$25.8 million have been received and will be used to retire existing debt, the company said.</p>
<p>The sale was to Knife River Dakota Inc, a subsidiary of MDU Resources Group Inc.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
